1800 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: What's wrong, David? The guys already left. You should have seen\them! They were wearing sunglasses and fake mustaches. I guess\celebrities can't go have fun like normal people, huh?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1810 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: Hi, Susanna. Sorry I woke you up last night.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1820 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: You...woke me up? I'm not sure I understand. I was dead tired after\yesterday's performance. I'm pretty sure I slept until 9 am, without\interruptions.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1830 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: But that's impossible. Don't you remember those people who got off\on the wrong floor?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1840 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: Are you sure that wasn't another dream? Maybe the pills didn't\work.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1850 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: ......":GOSUB 5100
1860 BM$="David couldn't believe that what had happened the previous night was\simply a dream. Which part was real? Which part was a dream? Did he\actually meet the ghost of that old man?":GOSUB 5100:BM$="The more he thought about it, the crazier everything felt...":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1870 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: David, calm down! You'll lose your mind if you don't relax. Come on,\tell me what happened last night...":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1880 GOSUB 6180:BM$="David could no longer keep it all to himself, so he showed Susanna the cloth\with the crest. He told her everything, starting from the old man.":GOSUB 5100:W5=0:RETURN
1890 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: It's definitely a nice crest. But... Something that leaves your\dreams and enters reality... That's scary to think of.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1900 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: As long as I have this in the real world, I'll have to grant that old\man's wish, even if it happens only in my dream.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1910 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: Maybe you can learn something by finding out more about this\crest. There has to be some kind of reference book about coats of arms at\the library.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1920 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: I didn't think of that! But I don't know Italian at all. Can you come with\me, Susanna?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1930 GOSUB 6340:BM$="Susanna: Of course! It'll be like a date. I'm looking forward to it!":GOSUB 5100
